From 28016d77271943783528a090f377e02f3a91123a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:30:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support GNU C++20

Build the libretro core with -std=gnu++20, so that AppleClang 15 with a
macOS 11 deployment target and the Android NDK r28c can build it.

- Replace C++23 language and library features: #elifdef, the UZ literal
  suffix, lambdas without a parameter clause, std::to_underlying,
  std::unreachable, std::byteswap and basic_string::contains().
- Avoid what the libc++ of Xcode 15.2 lacks or only allows from macOS
  13.3 on: std::format, floating-point std::from_chars and std::to_chars,
  and basic_stringstream::view().
- Deduce BitmaskEnum arguments through the class template; Clang before
  19 cannot do it through an alias template.
